    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nWelcome to 4 Le Bas Terrace combining period elegance, modern style and a superb location, this deceptively spacious 4-bedroom family home is well set back from the road and presents a wonderful opportunity to acquire a very inviting, energy-efficient (C2) Victorian property on this quiet residential road, which connects Leinster Road and Effra Road.\nBehind its handsome red-brick façade, lies a beautiful home filled with great warmth and character, generous proportions and refined contemporary style. Offering an impressive 175 sqm / 1884 sqft approx. of well-appointed accommodation, Number 4 comprises of a bright hallway, two elegant reception rooms, which provide versatile living and entertaining space, a large kitchen / dining room and downstairs shower room, which are complemented by 4 bedrooms, 3 of which are very large double rooms, and a well-appointed contemporary family bathroom. \nThe gardens, both front and rear, have been tastefully landscaped with a lovely mix of formal and contemporary design. The walled and railed front garden features pedestrian access, a synthetic lawn with parterre hedging and discreet bin store. It is well screened by mature hedgerow borders. The rear garden is a veritable 'outdoor room' with a paved patio area accessed from both the dining area and family room. A low maintenance synthetic lawn is bordered by well-stocked flowerbeds planted with a variety of shrubs, flowering plants and pleached trees affording great privacy, all of which complement the cut-stone walls, trellis fencing and mellow-aged brick rear elevation.\nEnjoying a superbly convenient location in a vibrant and ever-popular neighbourhood, Number 4 is within close walking distance of Rathmines town centre, with its extensive range of social and essential amenities to include local shopping, restaurants, coffee shops, leisure facilities etc. not to mention a choice of excellent local junior and senior schools. Regular transport links are well catered for, and the city centre is a 20-minute stroll away. Local shopping at Harold's Cross is nearby whilst Ranelagh is a 15-minute walk away with its lively restaurant scene and boutiques. \nSure to be of appeal to a wide and discerning buyer pool, viewing of 4 Le Bas Terrace is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nFan light, hardwood herringbone flooring, antique-style radiator, coving, centre rose, arch, phone point, under stairs storage with water tank.\n\nGuest WC/Shower Room - \nTiled floor, part tiled walls, wash hand basin, wall mounted WC, tiled shower cubicle with handheld shower attachment and drophead shower\n\nLiving Room - \nElegant reception room will tall double glazed sash window with working shutters, coving, centre rose, contemporary open fireplace with basket inset, light oak herringbone flooring and TV point.\n\nFamily Room - \nA second generous reception room with handsome cast iron open fireplace, fitted shelving and workspace, light oat herringbone flooring, coving, French doors to rear patio and garden.\n\nKitchen / Dining Room - \nA very generous room. The kitchen features Shaker-style wall and floor units with stainless steel sink unit, countertops, integrated Electrolux fridge, separate freezer, Neff double oven, Neff 5 ring gas hob, Elica extractor fan, wine fridge, integrated Bosh dishwasher, plumbed for washing machine. Part tiled walls, large Velux window, tiled floor, French doors to rear garden. The dining area comfortably seats 8-10 with fitted bench seating and features a panelled wall, light oak herringbone flooring, and French door to rear patio.\n\nUpstairs - \n\n\nFirst floor return - \n\n\nLanding - \nCoving, antique-style radiator.\n\nBedroom 3 - \nBright single to rear with picture window\n\nFamily bathroom - \nFeaturing a contemporary suite with part-tiled walls and fully tiled floor, bath with shower attachment, wall mounted wash hand basin, wall mounted WC, large heated towel rail, opaque picture window, recessed lights.\n\nBedroom 2 - \nLarge double to rear with coving, extensive fitted wardrobes, picture window with plantation shutters, floating bookshelves.\n\nFirst floor Landing - \nCoving, picture window, skylight, stairs to return.\n\nBedroom 1 - \nA very fine principal bedroom, which spans the full width of the property and features two tall double glazed sash windows with working shutters, attic access with automatic Stira, wall to wall fitted wardrobes, vanity desk, attractive cast iron open fireplace, coving, centre rose.\n\nSecond Floor - \n\n\nBedroom 4 - \nAnother very fine, bright double with picture window, shelving, attic access with pull down Stira.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Very attractive 4-bedroom Victorian terraced home</li><li>Bright, spacious accommodation of 175 sqm / 1884 sqft approx.</li><li>Refurbished and modernised with C2 BER</li><li>2 generous reception rooms</li><li>Large kitchen/dining room </li><li>4 bedrooms - 3 of which are large double rooms</li><li>Contemporary family bathroom and shower room</li><li>Landscaped front and rear gardens incorporating both modern and formal design</li><li>A quiet residential road linking Leinster Road and Effra Road</li><li>Superbly convenient location close to schools, shops, cafés, leisure amenities and transport facilities</li><li>Features include: GFCH; Double-glazed windows; Oak herringbone flooring; beautiful original detailing - coving, centre pieces etc. </li><li>On-street permit parking</ul>"
      },
